Third-party software redistributed by this repository
================================================================================

Every task under tasks/ carries one upstream open-source release, unmodified, in
environment/original.tar.gz.  That archive is State A: the tree the benchmark
asks a model to evolve.  The Apache-2.0 licence above covers this repository's
own work -- the shared grader in infra/, the task definitions, the per-task
ladders, the documentation.  It does not cover the vendored releases.  Each one
stays under its own terms, and its full licence text travels inside its own
archive, at the path named below (relative to the archive's root directory).

These entries were read out of the archives, not transcribed from the task
prose, and each licence file was compared byte-for-byte against its upstream
project at the recorded ref: 25 of 25 reachable files matched exactly.  The two
that are not on GitHub -- SQLite and QuickJS -- are recorded from the archive
alone.  Two checks keep this table honest rather than merely written down:
infra/tests/test_licensing.py re-derives it from the archives on every run, so an
entry cannot silently go stale and a new task cannot be added without appearing
here; tools/verify_upstream_licences.py repeats the comparison against upstream,
and is what to run when a task is added or re-pinned.

The licence identifiers are SPDX.  "AND" means parts of one release are under
different terms; "OR" means the recipient chooses.

